# Agent instructions

This repo follows [dev-standard](.dev-standard/README.md) v{{VERSION}}.
Full rules live in `.dev-standard/standards/`. Load the file for the area you are touching.
Rule IDs (for example `SDD-001`) appear in hook and CI errors; look them up there.

## Workflow

1. **Brainstorm** a feature with `/brainstorm <slug> "problem"`. It creates `brainstorms/<slug>/brainstorm.html`. The user picks the direction and exports `brainstorms/<slug>/brainstorm.md` themselves.
2. **Specify** with Spec Kit: `/speckit.specify` with `brainstorm.md` as input. Right after Spec Kit creates `specs/NNN-slug/`, run `git mv brainstorms/<slug>/brainstorm.* specs/NNN-slug/` before editing `spec.md`. Then `/speckit.clarify`; the user sets `**Status**: Approved`. The spec documents merge to `main` in a documents-only PR from `NNN-slug` (BRA-004).
3. **Plan and tasks**: `/speckit.plan`, `/speckit.tasks`, `/speckit.analyze`.
4. **Implement** one task per branch, test first: branch `NNN-tTTT-slug` from the latest `main`, then `/speckit.implement`. Unfinished features stay behind a flag that defaults to off.
5. **Ship** each task as one draft PR with `/pr`.

Bug fixes (`fix/slug`) and chores (`chore/slug`) skip steps 1 to 3.

## MUST rules

### Agent conduct · [agent-conduct.md](.dev-standard/standards/agent-conduct.md)
- AGT-001 Read the spec, plan and `tasks.md` before editing code.
- AGT-002 Never bypass checks: no `--no-verify`, no unexplained `eslint-disable` or `# noqa`, no skipped tests.
- AGT-003 Run format, lint, typecheck and tests before saying a task is done. Report results as they are.
- AGT-004 Never change a test assertion to make it pass without saying why in the PR.
- AGT-005 Stay inside the current task. Put anything else in the PR's follow-up list.

### Brainstorm and specs · [brainstorm.md](.dev-standard/standards/brainstorm.md) · [sdd.md](.dev-standard/standards/sdd.md)
- BRN-001 A feature spec starts from a `brainstorm.md` with `status: decided`.
- BRN-002 Propose at least 5 materially different options, including a do-nothing baseline.
- BRN-003 Set the appetite before scoring options.
- BRN-004 Never mark a direction as decided or write a decided `brainstorm.md`. Recommend; the user chooses and exports.
- SDD-001 No source edits on a feature branch (`NNN-slug`) until `spec.md` says `**Status**: Approved`.
- SDD-002 Write functional requirements as EARS sentences.
- SDD-003 Every requirement ID (`NNN/FR-002`) is referenced by at least one test.
- SDD-004 `plan.md` includes design-doc sections: alternatives considered and cross-cutting concerns.
- SDD-005 `/speckit.analyze` reports no critical issues before implementation.
- SDD-006 Scope changes go back through `/speckit.clarify`.

### Code · [naming.md](.dev-standard/standards/naming.md) · [code-style.md](.dev-standard/standards/code-style.md)
- NAM-001 Follow the casing table for the file's language.
- NAM-002 Functions start with a verb. NAM-004 Booleans start with `is`, `has`, `can` or `should`.
- NAM-003 Numbers with a unit carry it in the name: `timeoutMs`, `voltage_mv`.
- NAM-005 Write acronyms as words: `HttpClient`, `userId`.
- NAM-006 No `I` prefixes, no Hungarian notation, no abbreviations outside `id url api db io ctx`.
- NAM-007 Records: `brainstorms/<slug>/`, `specs/NNN-slug/`, `docs/adr/NNNN-slug.md`.
- STY-001 The formatter is the style. Never hand-format.
- STY-002 Strictest compiler and type-checker mode.
- STY-004 No magic numbers. STY-005 Comments say why; every TODO links an issue: `TODO(#123)`.

### Git, branches, PRs, review · [git.md](.dev-standard/standards/git.md) · [branching.md](.dev-standard/standards/branching.md) · [pull-requests.md](.dev-standard/standards/pull-requests.md) · [code-review.md](.dev-standard/standards/code-review.md)
- GIT-001 Conventional Commits, 72-character header max.
- GIT-002 The commit body says what and why. Footer: `Refs:`, `BREAKING CHANGE:`.
- GIT-004 Short-lived branches off `main`. GIT-005 Never commit to or force-push `main`.
- BRA-001 `main` is the only long-lived branch. BRA-002 One task per branch, merged within 3 days.
- BRA-003 Branches: `NNN-slug` spec docs, `NNN-tTTT-slug` one task, `fix/slug`, `chore/slug`, `docs/slug`, `release/vX.Y`.
- BRA-004 Merge the spec before the code; unfinished work ships behind a flag that defaults to off.
- BRA-006 Releases are `vX.Y.Z` tags on `main`. Fix on `main` first, then `git cherry-pick -x` to a release branch.
- BRA-011 Never `gh pr merge --admin`, and never change rulesets or branch protection.
- PR-001 PR title is a Conventional Commit line. PR-003 Fill every section of the PR template.
- PR-004 One self-contained change; refactors in their own PR. PR-005 Tests ship with the code.
- PR-006 Open as draft until CI is green. Squash merge.
- REV-004 An agent-written PR needs a human approval.

### Docs, decisions, tests · [documentation.md](.dev-standard/standards/documentation.md) · [decisions.md](.dev-standard/standards/decisions.md) · [testing.md](.dev-standard/standards/testing.md)
- DOC-003 / ADR-001 Hard-to-reverse decisions get an ADR in `docs/adr/` (MADR), one decision per file.
- ADR-008 Before proposing a design, read the accepted ADRs for that area. Don't contradict one without proposing a superseding ADR.
- ADR-005 Draft ADRs as `proposed`; only the user accepts. ADR-004 Never rewrite an accepted ADR; supersede it.
- ADR-006 The ADR lands with or before the change it decides. ADR-007 Update `docs/adr/README.md`.
- DOC-004 Public functions and modules have docstrings or TSDoc with an example.
- TST-001 A bug fix starts with a failing test that reproduces it.
- TST-002 Classify tests as small, medium or large. TST-003 Changed lines reach 80% coverage.
- TST-004 Any behavior you want kept, including config, has a test.

### Security and errors · [security.md](.dev-standard/standards/security.md) · [errors-logging.md](.dev-standard/standards/errors-logging.md)
- SEC-001 Never commit secrets. SEC-002 Commit lockfiles. SEC-003 Validate input at trust boundaries.
- SEC-005 Never run destructive commands (`rm -rf`, force push, `DROP`) without the user's confirmation.
- ERR-001 Never catch and ignore. ERR-002 Structured logs, no secrets or personal data.

{{#if react-web}}
### Frontend · [frontend.md](.dev-standard/standards/frontend.md)
- UI-001 React + TypeScript strict. Vite by default; Next.js only for SEO or server rendering.
- UI-002 Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, lucide-react, Recharts. Other UI libraries need an ADR.
- UI-003 Design tokens only: no raw hex values or arbitrary Tailwind values in components.
- UI-004 Rules of React; `react-hooks` and `jsx-a11y` lint at error.
- UI-005 TanStack Query for server state; React Hook Form + Zod for forms; API types generated from the backend's OpenAPI.
- UI-006 Feature folders: `src/features/<name>/`. UI-007 WCAG 2.2 AA, axe in Playwright.
- UI-008 Core Web Vitals at p75: LCP ≤ 2.5 s, INP ≤ 200 ms, CLS ≤ 0.1.
- UI-009 Vitest + Testing Library, Playwright, MSW. UI-010 Never store auth tokens in `localStorage`.
{{/if}}

{{#if deployed}}
### Production · [production/](.dev-standard/standards/production/README.md)
- AUTH-001 No home-made auth or crypto. Use the OIDC provider ({{AUTH_PROVIDER}}).
- AUTH-006 Check authorization on the server for every request and every object, deny by default.
- ABU-001 Rate limit every public endpoint per IP and per user in a shared store. ABU-003 Return `429` with `Retry-After`.
- API-001 Contract first: OpenAPI in `specs/NNN-slug/contracts/`. API-003 Errors are RFC 9457 problem details.
- WEB-002 Security headers per OWASP. WEB-005 Parameterized queries only; SSRF allowlist for outbound calls.
- REL-001 Twelve-factor. REL-003 Every network call has a timeout; retry only idempotent calls with backoff and jitter.
- REL-004 Migrations are versioned and follow expand and contract.
- OBS-001 OpenTelemetry. OBS-004 Every alert links a runbook.
- OPS-005 Secrets come from a secret manager. OPS-007 Pass the production readiness review (`docs/prr.md`) before first launch.
- DAT-001 Classify every field in `data-model.md`. DAT-005 Never log personal data, tokens or secrets.
{{/if}}

## Definition of done

A task is done only when all of these are true:

- [ ] Format, lint, typecheck and tests pass locally. The fast suite is `checks.fast` in `.dev-standard.json` (`{{FAST_CHECK_COMMAND}}`); the Stop hook runs it too.
- [ ] Source edits stayed under `paths.source` in `.dev-standard.json` (default `src/`, `app/`) only after the spec was approved; the require-spec hook guards those paths.
- [ ] Every requirement the task covers has a passing test that names its ID.
- [ ] Docs, ADRs and the changelog entry are updated in the same change.
- [ ] The task is ticked in `tasks.md`.
- [ ] A draft PR exists with every template section filled.

## Repo-specific conventions

Recorded at install from this repo's existing code. Keep them when you change existing code (INS-004).

